  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HABITAT RESTORATION &amp; ENHANCEMENT FOR WA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will: 1) Restore (2,050) hectares/(5063.5) acres of seasonal wetlands as migratory..waterfowl and shorebird habitat in the Santiaguillo Lagoon. 2) Sign conservation agreement with the..State Secretariat of Environment and Natural Resources for the conservation of 16,459..hectares/40,653.73 acres of Laguna Santiaguillo for at least 15 years. 3) Construct and rehabilitate..sewage systems and install 100 dry toilets in rural communities to reduce organic pollutant runoff in..the Santiaguillo lagoon watershed. 4) Train 120 teachers and reach 1,800 students in themes related to..wetlands conservation and train 100 ranchers in alternative farming techniques. 5) Assess habitat..quality by surveying productivity (aquatic invertebrates) in the restored areas, survey waterfowl and..shorebirds to determine habitat use, and analyze water quality in the northern section of the lagoon.</narrative>
  </description>
